WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.440
(KuroKy talking)

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.500
What are the qualities that make a good leader?

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.460
Perseverance.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.360
Dedication.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.560
Intelligence.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:38.220
The will to be nothing less than the best.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:43.649
Kuro “KuroKy” Salehi Takhasomi has all
of these qualities and more.

00:00:43.649 --> 00:00:48.780
He dreamed of being the best, of hoisting
the Aegis of Champions at The International.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.960
Not for money, not for glory, but for the
thrill of competition, to satisfy his desire

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.800
to lead a team to the top and win.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.760
But there always seemed to be something missing,
something not quite right: the timing,

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.920
his confidence, his team.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:10.040
He always had it in him, the potential to
be a true leader, a great player, a TI champion.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.760
But the journey was far from easy.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.880
This is his story.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.300
KuroKy was born in Iran, but grew up in Berlin,
Germany.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:24.040
A medical condition kept him from being an
active child, and as a result he gained

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.580
a love of video games.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.900
Once he discovered Dota, he was fully drawn
in, and, possessed by a fierce competitive spirit.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.080
By his mid teens he was already a tremendously
talented player.

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:51.280
In 2008, still just 16 years old, KuroKy would
join mousesports, and his Dota career began

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:52.409
in earnest.

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:57.409
He was a deadly and versatile core with a
strong mind for the game, renowned for his

00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:02.539
Mirana and Morphling, able to play both the
hard carry and mid lane role.

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:07.310
With Kuro, Mouz became one of the teams to
beat in the world, and that year he won the

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:12.700
prestigious GosuGamers “Carry of the Year”
by more than half the vote.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:18.209
With success and recognition fueling his dream
to be the best, Kuro found a kindred spirit

00:02:18.209 --> 00:02:22.230
in Clement “Puppey” Ivaonov, who helped
him take the next step.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:28.680
The two first met when Puppey acted as a standin
on mousesports, and they formed a fast friendship.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:33.841
In fact, Kuro was “overwhelmed” by how
similar his and Puppey’s goals were, as

00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:36.530
well as their way of thinking about the game.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.129
Together they resolved to create a new team.

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:44.189
The result was Kingsurf.International, who
made their debut at the DotA-League Masters

00:02:44.189 --> 00:02:45.579
2009.

00:02:45.579 --> 00:02:50.569
Despite one of their players, Vigoss, being
unable to sort out his visa in time for the

00:02:50.569 --> 00:02:55.700
tournament, Puppey and KuroKy’s faith in
each other was unwavering, and Kingsurf won

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.600
the event over Meet Your Makers.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.420
Kingsurf.Int continued to develop into one
of the best teams in Europe, and with Puppey

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:14.489
as their leader and KuroKy as the right-hand
man, they posted strong results across a number

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:16.370
of tournaments in 2009.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:21.269
But by the final months of 2009, KuroKy’s
motivation was slipping.

00:03:21.269 --> 00:03:26.360
He decided he needed a change, and so he joined
Meet Your Makers, where he took on a leadership

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.959
role in his own right.

00:03:27.959 --> 00:03:33.510
At first, the change was fantastic: MYM were
a dominant force in the scene, and KuroKy

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.620
was once again motivated to win.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:45.540
However, just a few months later, a very poor
result at SMM 2009 shattered KuroKy’s newfound

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.580
confidence.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:51.579
He realized he was not yet ready to lead
a team on his own, and thus joined Puppey’s

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:52.939
new squad.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:55.520
For the next year or so the team was a serious contender,

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.100
but the results were not good enough for Puppey,

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.080
who wanted nothing short of perfection.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:06.790
So when Natus Vincere contacted Puppey in
mid-2011 to join their team, KuroKy was confronted

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:08.719
with a difficult decision.

00:04:08.719 --> 00:04:13.791
He knew that if he asked Puppey to stay he
would, but he also knew he could not hold

00:04:13.791 --> 00:04:15.430
him back from the opportunity.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:21.010
Puppey asked KuroKy to keep playing without
him, but secretly KuroKy was planning on disappearing

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:21.840
from the scene.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.520
But, when he contacted the other members of
the team, they wanted to carry on with KuroKy

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.740
as their new captain.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:33.700
With renewed dedication, he led them into
the Dota 2 age and The International 2011.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:36.680
But there, they did not win a single match.

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:46.740
For the next six months, KuroKy largely stayed
away from the scene, occasionally playing

00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:47.880
here or there.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:53.390
However, his desire to win a TI and his passion
for competition slowly brought him back.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:58.650
He played for Virtus.pro as the team attempted
to qualify for The International 2012, but

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:00.900
they failed to make it to the event.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:06.740
However, KuroKy was given a second chance:
mousesports’ ComeWithMe was unable to attend

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.180
TI2, and KuroKy was asked to stand in at support.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.580
He accepted.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:32.240
While Mouz would finish in last place at TI2,
the chance to play at TI once again reignited

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:33.880
KuroKy’s drive to play.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:38.251
KuroKy would wind up sticking with mousesports
for the rest of the year, his mind for the

00:05:38.251 --> 00:05:43.030
game and flexibility proving valuable as he
played a number of roles.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:48.060
Despite mousesports rarely making it out of
group stages, KuroKy was back in full swing

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.590
and regaining his confidence.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:56.200
Over on Na`Vi, two slots had opened up following
the departure of LightofHeaven and ARS-ART.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:01.210
Puppey offered KuroKy the chance to play support
for Na`Vi — he accepted, reconnecting with

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:04.000
his partner in crime after more than a year.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:08.970
With his friend leading him once again, his
skills put to good use on an elite team and

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:14.640
his drive to win returned. KuroKy on Na`Vi
had a resurgence in 2013.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:19.860
A few months after adding KuroKy, Na`Vi were
firing on all cylinders.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:25.110
With Puppey’s leadership and drafting supplemented
by KuroKy’s knowledge, Na`Vi were widely

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.300
considered to be a serious contender at TI3.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:33.750
For the first time in three years, Kuroky
had a real shot at achieving Dota 2 glory.

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.080
Na`Vi made the most of the opportunity.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:07:13.400
(Commentators Casting)

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:18.280
Na`Vi tore through the event, fighting their
way into the grand finals and a showdown with

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.220
their biggest rival, Alliance.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:26.120
(Commentators Casting)

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:30.360
With all ten players playing at their peak
level, it was one of the greatest series of

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.840
Dota ever played.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:08:54.340
(Commentators Casting)

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.720
So close, and yet so far.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:02.620
KuroKy had been just one game away from fulfilling
his dream, but in a devastating Game 5,

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.900
he and Na`Vi fell just short.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:07.780
Despite the Aegis of Champions remaining elusive,

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.600
it was clear KuroKy’s pro Dota career had reached new heights.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:17.240
He gave his share of Na`Vi’s 632 thousand
dollar prize winnings to his parents.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:26.800
(KuroKy talking)

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.880
But for KuroKy, it never was really about the money.

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:35.540
(KuroKy talking)

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.280
And for many years, he studied psychology in addition to playing competitively.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:44.760
Na`Vi stuck together, and closed out 2013
winning five tournaments.

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:50.700
They continued their strong form for the first
few months of 2014, but by March, cracks were

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:51.970
beginning to show.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:56.030
Na`Vi’s play suffered, and their results
dipped sharply.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:10:03.060
By the time TI4 rolled around, an early exit
at 7-8th place was not a surprise, even for KuroKy.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:14.180
(KuroKy talking)

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.400
After two years on Na`Vi, it was time for
a change.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:22.800
However, KuroKy wanted to remain with Puppey,
and so he joined him at his new project, a

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:26.140
player-founded org which would be called Team
Secret.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:30.780
As part of the new roster, KuroKy returned
to the carry role, proving his skills were

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.560
not rusty in the slightest.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:45.720
(Commentators Casting)

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:51.370
However, while Secret posted solid results
right off the bat, Puppey’s desire for perfection

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:53.430
would cause rifts in the team.

00:10:53.430 --> 00:10:59.450
Fly left the team, followed by n0tail, to
eventually be replaced by Evil Geniuses’ Arteezy

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:00.450
and Zai.

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:04.420
The move pushed KuroKy back into the support
role, but the results would prove to be well

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:06.020
worth the sacrifice.

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:12.880
After a rocky start at both DAC 2015 and StarLadder
StarSeries Season 12, Secret would go on to

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:18.080
win four of the five events they attended
leading up to TI5, marking them as a clear

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:20.000
favorite to win the Aegis.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.240
The team was skilled, smart, and had momentum.

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.850
This time, surely, KuroKy would be victorious.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:55.560
(Commentators Casting)

00:11:55.560 --> 00:12:01.760
The fallout was inevitable, with many pointing
fingers at KuroKy, especially Arteezy.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:11.280
(Talking)

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:17.640
KuroKy shouldered some of the blame, especially
for his play at TI5, but also stated he was

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:19.960
the scapegoat for the team’s failure.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:23.980
With both sides digging in their heels, a
split was unavoidable.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:29.630
Arteezy left to return to Evil Geniuses, and
KuroKy decided it was time to move on.

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:34.290
While there was no bad blood between Puppey
and KuroKy, it was the opportunity for KuroKy

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:38.490
to build something of his own and take another
shot at leadership.

00:12:38.490 --> 00:12:40.820
This time, KuroKy was finally ready.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:45.160
He led his team with a firm belief in the mental aspect of the game.

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:59.600
(KuroKy talking)

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:03.780
In essence, KuroKy had shifted focus from
being the “core” of his team’s gameplay

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:06.000
to a different sort of core.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:17.520
(KuroKy talking)

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:21.300
An emotional
and strategic bedrock upon which his team could rely.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:29.220
(KuroKy talking)

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:34.980
With these philosophies in hand, KuroKy set
about building his new team, dubbed 5Jungz.

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:38.640
He sought out young players with tremendous
talent. He selected:

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:44.360
FATA-, MATUMBAMAN, JerAx and MinD_ContRoL,
and forged ahead in making his new hand-picked

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:45.940
squad a contender.

00:13:45.940 --> 00:13:50.660
Even after being picked up by Team Liquid,
KuroKy and Co. posted a mixed bag of results

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:52.460
for the remainder of 2015.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:14:02.680
(KuroKy talking)

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:07.440
By early 2016 KuroKy’s dedication and patience
was starting to show dividends.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:11.760
It all finally came together in March, where
the team put on a sensational performance

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:16.820
at The Shanghai Major, culminating in a showdown
against Puppey’s new-look Team Secret.

00:14:17.120 --> 00:15:02.520
(Commentators Casting)

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:07.180
In just six months, KuroKy had led a brand
new squad to challenge his old friend’s

00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:10.180
super-star roster in the Grand Finals of a Major.

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:14.360
While the end result was disappointing, it
was validation for KuroKy’s leadership style,

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:18.300
effort and decision to split from Puppey and
create something of his own.

00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:22.240
Liquid kept at it, becoming an elite force
in the European scene.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:26.220
KuroKy was learning more and more about being
a captain and a leader as the players under

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:28.380
him grew more and more experienced and

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.380
comfortable with his new system.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:36.340
Wins at EPICENTER 2016 and 2nd place at the
Manila Major were the rewards for their efforts.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:39.300
Finally, it was time to face TI6.

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:43.480
While a few of the players had never before
played on Dota 2’s biggest stage, KuroKy

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:46.460
and Liquid were still confident they could
make a splash.

00:15:46.460 --> 00:15:48.760
Things however, did not go according to plan.

00:15:48.760 --> 00:16:10.400
(Commentators Casting)

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:12.720
Clearly, something still was not quite right.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:17.260
KuroKy had learned much in his first year
as a full captain, but the Aegis was once

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.480
again out of reach.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:23.310
He did not give up: Liquid was his team,
his players — they needed him to keep going,

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.399
keep teaching them.

00:16:24.399 --> 00:16:26.270
He knew they could get there.

00:16:26.270 --> 00:16:31.260
But first, a roster change was in order — FATA-
decided to step away from the scene for a

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.680
while and JerAx left for OG.

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:37.890
In a blockbuster move, Liquid picked up one
of the hottest players in the scene...

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:38.940
Miracle-.

00:16:38.940 --> 00:16:43.240
A few months later, GH- was brought in as
the final piece of the puzzle.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:47.880
With the new roster in place, KuroKy had everything
he needed to finally reach the top.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:58.360
(Talking)

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:01.960
Liquid surged to the top of the pack, and
they began to win.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:03.240
A lot.

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:07.980
KuroKy received heaps of praise for his steadfast
leadership, drafting savvy and relentless

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.520
work ethic as Liquid racked up the hardware.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:26.540
(Nazgul talking)

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:31.299
With such a dynamic and skilled team, he was not
going to let this chance slip away.

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:33.900
And then, it was time.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:40.700
The International 2017 — everything KuroKy
had done in the past two years, everything

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.560
he had learned and worked for had lead him here.

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.500
In the group stage, Liquid looked unstoppable.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:18:24.080
(Commentators Casting)

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.400
But then, their confidence got to them.

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:46.740
(Commentators Casting)

00:18:46.740 --> 00:18:50.200
KuroKy was not pleased — but Liquid had
another shot.

00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:53.720
They were staring down the long, difficult
road of the lower bracket.

00:18:53.720 --> 00:18:56.840
KuroKy did not allow his team to misstep again.

00:18:56.840 --> 00:19:22.780
(Commentators Casting)

00:19:22.789 --> 00:19:27.289
The last time he was here, KuroKy had had
his dream ripped away from him.

00:19:27.289 --> 00:19:30.980
This time however, destiny called.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.860
This time was the right time.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:20:21.780
(Commentators Casting)

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:24.200
KuroKy was once again one game away.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:28.640
But even though he had it all in his hands,
he would not allow his team to lose focus.

00:20:28.640 --> 00:20:30.640
He knew the job was not done.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:21:52.500
(Commentators Casting)

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:58.139
After seven years of struggle, ups and downs,
shattered confidence and roster rebuilds,

00:21:58.139 --> 00:22:00.149
KuroKy had led a team to glory.

00:22:00.149 --> 00:22:01.659
He had finally succeeded.

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:04.820
He had won The International.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:09.320
Today, KuroKy and Liquid are still working and still winning.

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:13.600
Having achieved his dream, KuroKy has now set
his sights on repeating as a TI champion.

00:22:13.600 --> 00:22:16.840
He’s one of only three players to attend every TI.

00:22:16.840 --> 00:22:22.039
He’s won the most money of any esports player
ever, but like we learned before, for KuroKy

00:22:22.039 --> 00:22:23.379
it’s not about the money.

00:22:23.379 --> 00:22:27.289
There’s a reason after all these years,
all the heartbreak and all the struggles,

00:22:27.289 --> 00:22:28.700
he’s kept going.

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:33.080
Still, as it’s always been, it’s about
the thrill of victory, the love of competition

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:35.760
and the joy of leading a band of brothers forward.

00:22:35.760 --> 00:22:36.760
Perseverance.

00:22:36.760 --> 00:22:37.760
Dedication.

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:38.760
Intelligence.

00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:41.179
The will to be nothing but the best.

00:22:41.179 --> 00:22:42.980
These are what define a true leader.

00:22:42.980 --> 00:22:44.740
These are what define a Dota legend.

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:47.080
These are what define KuroKy.

